(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Types made from specs and the objects C makes (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"; the user's"] [4 1 "// 262 DECISION (a)): PyType_FromMetaclass and its three entries (FromSpec, FromSpecWithBases, FromModuleAndSpec),"] [5 1 "// PyType_GetSlot, the relative offsets of PEP 697 (PyObject_GetTypeData, PyType_GetTypeDataSize, Py_RELATIVE_OFFSET's"] [6 1 "// members), PyType_GenericAlloc and PyType_GenericNew, PyMember_GetOne and PyMember_SetOne, ported from CPython"] [7 1 "// 3.14.10's Objects/typeobject.c and Python/structmember.c (the PSF's license, LICENSE.md)."] [8 1 "//"] [9 1 "// A type made from a spec is a pyi type (NewExtType: static to pyi, its instances of a layout of their own, so a class"] [10 1 "// deriving from it keeps a C-born value as a class deriving from a built-in type does) whose slots call the spec's C"] [11 1 "// functions, and whose methods, members and getsets are descriptors that call C or read the instance's memory. Its"] [12 1 "// instances are C-born: their memory is the world's (tp_basicsize bytes, malloc'd, the PyObject head first), their"] [13 1 "// handle is that memory's address, and their ob_refcnt counts C's references as a proxy's does (world.go). Python's"] [14 1 "// references are Go's: the Go value (cObj) is in the handles' maps while C holds a reference or a C entry is in"] [15 1 "// progress (as a proxy is), and once it is Python's alone and Go collects it, its type's tp_dealloc runs (on the C"] [16 1 "// world's next entry, as cbuf's free): the C memory lives exactly as long as both sides need it."] [30 1 "// tp_flags (Include/object.h)"] [43 1 "// fullyQualifiedName is _PyType_GetFullyQualifiedName (PyErr_Format's %N): module.qualname, the module left out for"] [44 1 "// builtins and __main__ (queue 270b)."] [54 1 "// metaCustomNew is a metaclass's tp_new other than type's (PyType_FromMetaclass refuses it, queue 270b): a C type's"] [55 1 "// own tp_new