object at addr (its memory's, of ct's layout), in the handles' maps."] [230 1 "// asCObj is the C-born object o is or keeps (nil: none)."] [246 1 "// cHandle is the handle of a C-born object: its address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the C entry"] [247 1 "// ends) when it had left them."] [259 1 "// pyOf is the Python object of a C-born object (the instance that keeps it, else itself)."] [267 1 "// reapDead deallocates the C-born objects Go collected (outside any C entry, before the next one)."] [275 13 "// a new object at the same address (cannot be: the memory was not freed) or still C's"] [281 1 "// dealloc is the object's tp_dealloc (its type's, a C base's, else subtype_dealloc's: the dict its memory holds"] [282 1 "// released, the memory freed), run with a Go value in the maps for the natives it calls."] [311 24 "// an instance over a built-in base (queue 269)"] [317 1 "// subtypeDealloc is subtype_dealloc for a C-born object (Objects/typeobject.c): the dict at tp_dictoffset released,"] [318 1 "// the memory freed (tp_free, PyObject_Free); the type is immortal to the handles (its reference left alone)."] [330 1 "// objectFree is PyObject_Free: the memory freed, a C-born object's Go value out of the maps."] [342 1 "// writeUnraisable reports a tp_dealloc's error as CPython's PyErr_WriteUnraisable does."] [345 1 "// genericAlloc is PyType_GenericAlloc (_PyType_AllocNoTrack): basicsize + (nitems+1) * itemsize bytes of the world,"] [346 1 "// zeroed, the head initialized (a new reference: ob_refcnt 1), its ob_size nitems for a variable-size type."] [371 3 "// a class deriving from the C type: the instance keeps the object, its memory names the class"] [377 1 "// ---- calling C ----"] [381 1 "// ccallT calls the C function fn with pointer-sized arguments; its result as ret (TPointer, TSInt32, TSInt64)."] [410 1 "// cEnter brackets a slot's call into C: the error indicator cleared, a missing native's panic its error."] [411 1 "// Usage: defer cExit(cEnter(), &err)."] [430 1 "// objResult is the object a C function returned (a new reference, stolen), or the error it set."] [449 1 "// intResult is an int a C function returned, -1 with the error it set."] [459 1 "// cAddrOf is the handle C gets for o (a C-born object's address)."] [467 1 "// ---- the slots ----"] [469 1 "// slot is the type's slot id: its spec's, a C base's (inherit_slots), else 0."] [480 1 "// fillSlots makes the spec's slots the type's: each pyi slot calls its C function."] [484 39 "// a metaclass (queue 270b): its instances are pyi types, not wrapped values"] [488 27 "// a built-in base's (queue 269): each takes the instance's built-in value"] [587 2 "// nb_divmod (queue 525): divmod's slot, the reflected call with the operands swapped back (slot wrappers"] [588 2 "// __divmod__ and __rdivmod__)"] [593 2 "// nb_power with a modulus (queue 525): ternary_op calls it for each operand whose type has it, C checking the types"] [617 2 "// __ipow__(other, mod=None): wrap_ternaryfunc's optional modulo reaches nb_inplace_power (test_misc's ipowType)"] [658 3 "// tp_setattr, the name a char * (slot_tp_setattro's older twin; xxlimited_35's Xxo_setattr, py-eval-1122)"] [681 2 "// tp_new: the spec's (a C base's), else object's (tp_alloc, object_new's checks); tp_init: the spec's"] [684 3 "// type's own __new__ (the metaclass's instances made by type_new), unless instantiation is disallowed"] [735 4 "// the base's __new__ makes the built-in value from the arguments (queue 270b), its memory C's"] [770 1 "// bufferWrappers are a C type's __buffer__ and __release_buffer__ (Objects/typeobject.c's wrap_buffer and"] [771 1 "// wrap_releasebuffer over bf_getbuffer and bf_releasebuffer; queue 473): a memoryview of the type's Py_buffer for"] [772 1 "// flags, and its release."] [800 1 "// argsTupleDict are the positional arguments' tuple and the keywords' dict (nil: none) of a vectorcall's arguments."] [814 1 "// callCObj calls a C-born object: its vectorcall (Py_T